msgid "NPU高性能编程指南"
msgstr "NPU High-Performance Programming Guide"

msgid "本文档介绍NPU高性能编程，涵盖合并Grid分核、指令并行优化、数据类型优化三类优化原则与配套Triton算子代码示例，适用于将Triton算子从GPU迁移至NPU并进行性能调优的开发者。"
msgstr "This document introduces high-performance NPU programming. It covers three optimization principles: merged Grid core partitioning, instruction parallel optimization, and data type optimization. It also provides corresponding Triton operator code examples. If you are migrating Triton operators from GPUs to NPUs and performing performance tuning, this document is for you."

msgid "合并Grid分核"
msgstr "Merge Grid core splitting"

msgid "一、自动合并Grid分核优化原则"
msgstr "1\\. Automatic Grid Merging and Core Partitioning Optimization Principles"

msgid "部分场景需要将Triton算子从GPU迁移到NPU。由于体系结构差异，基于GPU开发的Triton算子通常具有较大的逻辑grid，无法在NPU上一次全部调度。昇腾后端会自动把符合条件且逻辑核相互独立的任务映射到可用物理核，并根据IR安全分析跳过不适用的Kernel。性能调优时应先检查grid大小和编译告警；如果自动mapping被跳过，需要通过显式Tiling或内层循环减小逻辑grid。"
msgstr "In some scenarios, you need to migrate Triton operators from the GPU to the NPU. Due to architectural differences, Triton operators developed for the GPU typically have a large logical grid and cannot be fully scheduled on the NPU at once. The Ascend backend automatically maps eligible tasks with mutually independent logical cores to available physical cores, and skips inapplicable kernels based on IR safety analysis. When tuning performance, first check the grid size and compilation warnings; if automatic mapping is skipped, reduce the logical grid through explicit tiling or inner loops."

msgid "指令并行优化"
msgstr "Instruction Parallelism Optimization"

msgid "一、指令并行优化核心原则"
msgstr "1\\. Core Principles of Instruction Parallel Optimization"

msgid "Triton算子在NPU上执行时，为了提升性能，NPU底层提供multi buffer、指令并行等并行机制，将“数据搬入/数据计算/数据搬出”并行起来，以此来提升性能；但是某些场景下存在multi buffer无法使能问题，影响并行度，导致算子执行性能降低；在性能优化过程中，存在此类问题时，可以参考以下几点做排查，并按照代码示例优化： 1、数据搬运和计算存在数据依赖，产生同步，必须依赖Vector运算后，才能触发MTE搬运，导致并行度低； 2、算子内，无多个数据加载或者单次执行完成无Tiling切分，该场景下无法使能multi buffer； 3、multi buffer需要额外增加UB空间的使用量，计算过程中UB空间不足，无法使能multi buffer。"
msgstr "When a Triton operator runs on an NPU, the underlying NPU provides parallel mechanisms such as multi buffer and instruction parallelism to improve performance. These mechanisms parallelize \"data load/data compute/data store\" to improve performance. However, in certain scenarios, multi buffer cannot be enabled. This affects the parallelism and reduces the operator execution performance. During performance tuning, if you encounter these issues, refer to the following points for troubleshooting and optimize based on the code examples: 1. Data movement and computation have data dependencies, causing synchronization. The MTE data movement can be triggered only after the Vector computation is complete, resulting in low parallelism; 2. Within the operator, there are no multiple data loads or no tiling split after a single execution. In this scenario, multi buffer cannot be enabled; 3. Multi buffer requires additional UB space. If the UB space is insufficient during computation, multi buffer cannot be enabled."

