msgid "数据类型优化"
msgstr "Data Type Optimization"

msgid "一、数据类型优化核心原则"
msgstr "1\\. Core Principles of Data Type Optimization"

msgid "Atlas A2系列产品、Atlas A3系列产品向量运算单元的部分运算操作不支持某些数据类型，这种场景下，对应的向量运算会退化为标量运算，影响性能。在确保不影响整体算子精度的情况下，建议使用支持的数据类型，提升性能。 主要涉及以下操作："
msgstr "Some operations of the vector computing unit in Atlas A2 products and Atlas A3 products do not support certain data types. In this scenario, the corresponding vector operations degrade to scalar operations, affecting performance. Without affecting the overall operator precision, use supported data types to improve performance. The following operations are mainly involved:"

msgid "**OP名称**"
msgstr "**Operator name**"

msgid "**不支持的数据类型**"
msgstr "**Unsupported data types**"

msgid "Vector ADD"
msgstr "Vector ADD"

msgid "int64"
msgstr "int64"

msgid "Vector CMP"
msgstr "Vector CMP"

msgid "int64/int32"
msgstr "int64/int32"

msgid "Vector Add Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Vector Add Triton operator sample code"

msgid "如下Triton算子，当x、y两个input tensor使用int64数据类型时，x1+y1运算会展开为Scalar运算，从而降低性能。在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用int32数据类型。"
msgstr "For the following Triton operator, when the two input tensors x and y use the int64 data type, the x1+y1 operation is expanded into scalar operations, which reduces performance. If precision is not affected, use the int32 data type."

msgid ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def npu_vector_add_kernel(\n"
"    x,                          # [Tensor] input tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    y,                          # [Tensor] input tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    z,                          # [Tensor] output tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    vector_len: tl.constexpr,   # len of the vector\n"
"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr\n"
"):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n"
"    offset = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    len_mask = offset < vector_len\n"
"    x1 = tl.load(x + offset, mask=len_mask)\n"
"    y1 = tl.load(y + offset, mask=len_mask)\n"
"    z1 = x1 + y1\n"
"    tl.store(z + offset, z1, mask=len_mask)\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def npu_vector_add_kernel(\n"
"    x,                          # [Tensor] input tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    y,                          # [Tensor] input tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    z,                          # [Tensor] output tensor (1 x col)\n"
"    vector_len: tl.constexpr,   # len of the vector\n"
"    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr\n"
"):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n"
"    offset = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    len_mask = offset < vector_len\n"
"    x1 = tl.load(x + offset, mask=len_mask)\n"
"    y1 = tl.load(y + offset, mask=len_mask)\n"
"    z1 = x1 + y1\n"
"    tl.store(z + offset, z1, mask=len_mask)\n"

msgid "Vector Cmp Triton算子示例代码"
msgstr "Sample code for the Vector Cmp Triton operator"

msgid "如下Triton算子，做Mask运算时，使用到了Cmp操作，Cmp不支持int64/int32数据类型，会导致cols < N运算展开为Scalar运算，降低性能。在不影响精度的情况下，建议使用fp32数据类型。   在Triton算子编程中，Mask运算经常运用在load/store/where等语法中，在性能优化过程中，需要特别注意这类运算导致的性能下降。"
msgstr "In the following Triton operator, the mask operation uses the Cmp operation. Cmp does not support the int64 or int32 data types, causing the cols < N operation to expand into scalar operations and reducing performance. If precision is not affected, use the fp32 data type.   In Triton operator programming, mask operations are frequently used in syntaxes such as load, store, and where. During performance tuning, pay special attention to the performance degradation caused by such operations."

msgid ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def npu_vector_cmp_kernel(\n"
"    X,                 # [Tensor] input tensor (row x col)\n"
"    Out,               # [Tensor] output tensor (row x col)\n"
"    Mean,              # [Vector] mean tensor (row, ) of X\n"
"    Rstd,              # [Vector] std tensor (row, ) of X\n"
"    stride_x_row,      # [Scalar] stride of row of x\n"
"    stride_out_row,    # [Scalar] stride of row of out, normally equals to stride_x_row\n"
"    M,                 # [Scalar] row number\n"
"    N,                 # [Scalar] col number\n"
"    eps,               # [Scalar] epsilon to avoid division by zeros\n"
"    BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\n"
"    BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr\n"
"):\n"
"    group_m = tl.program_id(0)\n"
"    group_n = tl.program_id(1)\n"
"    row = group_m\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate index & offset\n"
"    Mean = Mean + group_n * M\n"
"    Rstd = Rstd + group_n * M\n"
"    X = X + row * stride_x_row + group_n * N\n"
"    Out = Out + row * stride_out_row + group_n * N\n"
"\n"
"    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)  # cols is int64\n"
"    x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=cols < N, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate mean & rstd\n"
"    mean = tl.sum(x, axis=0) / N\n"
"    tl.store(Mean + row, mean)\n"
"    # [Changed begin]\n"
"    # xbar = tl.where(cols < N, X - mean, 0.0)\n"
"    cols_cmp = cols.to(tl.float32)\n"
"    xbar = tl.where(cols_cmp < N, x - mean, 0.0)\n"
"    # [Changed end]\n"
"\n"
"    var = tl.sum(xbar * xbar, axis=0) / N\n"
"    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n"
"    tl.store(Rstd + row, rstd)\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate Out\n"
"    mask = cols < N\n"
"    out = (x - mean) * rstd\n"
"    tl.store(Out + cols, out, mask=mask)\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def npu_vector_cmp_kernel(\n"
"    X,                 # [Tensor] input tensor (row x col)\n"
"    Out,               # [Tensor] output tensor (row x col)\n"
"    Mean,              # [Vector] mean tensor (row, ) of X\n"
"    Rstd,              # [Vector] std tensor (row, ) of X\n"
"    stride_x_row,      # [Scalar] stride of row of x\n"
"    stride_out_row,    # [Scalar] stride of row of out, normally equals to stride_x_row\n"
"    M,                 # [Scalar] row number\n"
"    N,                 # [Scalar] col number\n"
"    eps,               # [Scalar] epsilon to avoid division by zeros\n"
"    BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\n"
"    BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr\n"
"):\n"
"    group_m = tl.program_id(0)\n"
"    group_n = tl.program_id(1)\n"
"    row = group_m\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate index & offset\n"
"    Mean = Mean + group_n * M\n"
"    Rstd = Rstd + group_n * M\n"
"    X = X + row * stride_x_row + group_n * N\n"
"    Out = Out + row * stride_out_row + group_n * N\n"
"\n"
"    cols = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)  # cols is int64\n"
"    x = tl.load(X + cols, mask=cols < N, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate mean & rstd\n"
"    mean = tl.sum(x, axis=0) / N\n"
"    tl.store(Mean + row, mean)\n"
"    # [Changed begin]\n"
"    # xbar = tl.where(cols < N, X - mean, 0.0)\n"
"    cols_cmp = cols.to(tl.float32)\n"
"    xbar = tl.where(cols_cmp < N, x - mean, 0.0)\n"
"    # [Changed end]\n"
"\n"
"    var = tl.sum(xbar * xbar, axis=0) / N\n"
"    rstd = 1 / tl.sqrt(var + eps)\n"
"    tl.store(Rstd + row, rstd)\n"
"\n"
"    # calculate Out\n"
"    mask = cols < N\n"
"    out = (x - mean) * rstd\n"
"    tl.store(Out + cols, out, mask=mask)\n"
